<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
<code>builtins.getEnv</code> reads an environment variable from the host running
Nix evaluation. That makes evaluation impure and host-dependent, and under
<code>--pure-eval</code> the call silently returns the empty string instead.
Values read this way can also leak into derivation hashes or generated outputs.
</p>
<p>
This is a Nix form of CWE-807: trusting mutable external input to influence
security-relevant or reproducibility-relevant behavior.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Avoid <code>builtins.getEnv</code> in reproducible Nix code. Pass required values
explicitly as function arguments, module options, or fixed string attributes so
that evaluation does not depend on the caller's shell environment.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Unsafe — reads <code>HOME</code> from the evaluator environment:</p>
<sample language="nix">
let
  home = builtins.getEnv "HOME";
in
...
</sample>
<p>Unsafe — bare <code>getEnv</code> under <code>with builtins;</code>:</p>
<sample language="nix">
with builtins;
getEnv "PATH"
</sample>
<p>Safe — thread the value explicitly instead of reading the environment:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ homeDir }:
let
  home = homeDir;
in
...
</sample>
<p>Safe — a different helper named <code>getEnv</code> in another namespace:</p>
<sample language="nix">
lib.getEnv "HOME"
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>
Nix Reference Manual:
<a href="https://nix.dev/manual/nix/latest/language/builtins#builtins-getEnv">builtins.getEnv</a>
</li>
<li>
CWE: <a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html">CWE-807: Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision</a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
